One record, read as a grant
Two columns. On the left, the usual arrangement: a record saying who works
here, a separate directory saying who may log in, and the day somebody who left
last year is still in the second one. On the right, one record carrying a
period — a nurse, in this department, from March until the end of August — read
directly as the grant. Revoking access is ending the period, on a record that
already had history.
